2. **[CONFIRMED] Reflexion loop produced 385 junk rules in 24h (70KB).**
   Evidence: `learned_rules.md` grew from 809 to 1,209 lines. All 385 new entries were generic
   "implement a volume check" / "ensure sufficient volume" noise.
   Root cause: `main.py:check_closed_trades()` blindly appended raw LLM `new_rule` output. The
   `generate_post_mortem()` prompt was too vague, producing generic advice.
   Fix: (a) Added rule validation with banned-phrase filter and min-length check. (b) Upgraded
   post-mortem prompt to reference existing tools and require symbol-specific rules. (c) Pruned
   file from 1,209 to 26 lines. (d) Added 100KB cap with auto-truncation.

3. **[CONFIRMED] No persistent chat/tool logging for chat.py and local_assistant.py.**
   Evidence: `conversation_history` lived only in memory, no disk persistence.
